{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338030-solo-character-help-also-new-spells","id":1338030,"title":"Solo Character Help (also new spells)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-26T13:41:33-07:00","id":1338030,"title":"Solo Character Help (also new spells)","content":"One of my friends and I are looking at starting a solo Exalted 3e campaign. We've done a ton of gaming together, both group and solo, so I'm not worried about that part. But we've only played about half a campaign of 3e, so while we've got a decent grasp on the basic rules, we're not too certain about potential pitfalls. So I come to you with two purposes: feedback on my character idea, and general advice for a solo campaign.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Three Silk Stars</u></b></div><br /> The basic concept is &quot;spirit-hunting scholar.&quot; She's an Occult-Supernal Twilight, built using the rules of &quot;experienced Exalts.&quot; She's meant to be a very quiet and nerdy and awkward and earnest young woman who just... happens to be ridiculously good with a sword for Reasons she refuses to explain. And who carries a couple of demons around in her anima for safekeeping. (My quote of reference is &quot;um, err, that's not... oh, <i>bother</i>. .&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Backstory</u></b><br /> Three Silk Stars was born to a minor branch of House Nellens. She never exalted, but was sent to the Cloister of Wisdom on an academic track\u2014she was meant to become an Immaculate priestess. There she learned some martial arts and thaumaturgy, as well as a great deal about spirits, divinity, and so on.<br /> <br /> At 16, was so sick of being taunted about her mortal status that she decided to cheat\u2014 she pieced together a bunch of spells she wasn\u2019t supposed to have access to and attempted to make contact with Hesiesh, the Immaculate Dragon of Fire, to plead her case. She only connected to a Lesser Dragon, Tarakhu, who was amused at her audacity and made a deal, granting her sorcerous powers.<br /> <br /> The blasphemy was quickly found out and she had to run. She barely managed to escape\u2014first the Imperial City, then the Blessed Isle, then the Scavenger Lands\u2026 she ran a long-ass way, is the point. Along the way, she worked sometimes as a teacher, sometimes as a priestess, sometimes as a scribe, and occasionally as an exorcist. Especially the last one; she built a mild reputation when she was far enough from the center of the Realm that she stopped hiding so much.<br /> <br /> On the boundaries of the Scavenger Lands, she found herself in a demon-haunted village. A strong demon. After weeks of work, she managed to deduce its true name and pull of a sorcerous working to banish it. She Exalted on the spot. She knew a little about the true nature of Solars, what with her background, and after Exalting spent years trying to figure out the truth about Exaltations, the Usurpation, the First Age, all that ****. She\u2019s figured out\u2026 some of it.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Build</u></b><br /> <i>Note: The GM has already okay'd me using slashing swords with White Reaper style. Makes more sense than spears anyway.</i><br /> <br /> <b><u>Attributes</u></b><br /> Strength 3<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 3<br /> Charisma 3<br /> Manipulation 2<br /> Appearance 2<br /> Perception 2<br /> Intelligence 4<br /> Wits 3<br /> <br /> <b><u>Abilities</u></b><br /> Athletics 2<br /> Awareness 4<br /> Brawl 1<br /> Dodge 3<br /> Integrity 2<br /> Linguistics 2<br /> Lore 4<br /> Martial Arts (White Reaper) 5<br /> Martial Arts (Single Point Shining into the Void) 5<br /> Occult 5<br /> Presence 2<br /> Resistance 4<br /> Socialize 2<br /> <br /> (Favored Abilities: Athletics, Awareness, Brawl/Martial Arts, Presence, Resistance)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Merits</u></b><br /> Martial Arts 4<br /> Languages 3 (High Realm, Old Ream, Riverspeak, Forestspeak)<br /> The Burning Name 2<br /> Artifact 2 (Yasal Crystal)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Specialties</u></b><br /> Martial Arts (White Reaper)<br /> Martial Arts (Single Point)<br /> Lore (Religion)<br /> Awareness (Join Battle)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Charms and Spells</u></b><br /> Falling Scythe Flash<br /> Revolving Crescent Defense<br /> White Reaper Form<br /> Bleeding Crescent Strike<br /> Flickering Corona Barrier<br /> Greatest Killer Attribute<br /> <br /> Gathering Light Concentration<br /> Shining Starfall Execution<br /> Single Point Shining Into The Void Form<br /> Horizon-Swallowed Star Flash<br /> <br /> Durability of Oak<br /> Spirit Strengthens Skin<br /> Iron Skin Concentration<br /> Ox Body Technique<br /> <br /> Spirit-Detecting Glance<br /> Spirit-Cutting Attack<br /> Ghost-Eating Technique<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery (Shaping Ritual: Pact with an Ifrit Lord)<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Flight of the Brilliant Raptor (Control Spell)<br /> Impenetrable Skin of Bronze<br /> Summon Elemental</div>Harmonious Academic Methodology<br /> Bottomless Wellspring Approach<br /> <br /> So yeah, that's it.... Thoughts? Advice? I've got two dots of merits and four bonus dots in reserve still... <br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> <br /> Also some ideas for new spells-- the former is meant to be an alternative to Flight of the Brilliant Raptor as her patron-granted control spell; the later is an adaptation of Claws of the Wood Dragon that fits her a bit better.<br /> <br /> <b>HESIESH\u2019S GIFT OF DIVINITY<br /> </b><b>Cost</b>: 15sm, 1 wp <br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Scene<br /> <br /> The sorcerer calls upon the great Immaculate Dragon of fire to cloak herself with raging flames, granting an assortment of benefits:<ul><li>She gains immunity to mundane heat hazards</li> <li>She may add her Essence to her soak and hardness against fire attacks.</li> <li>Her unarmed strikes gain the lethal and flame tags, and deal additional damage equal to her Essence.</li> <li>She may add her Essence to the damage she inflicts with mundane and magical fire attacks. This bonus is already included in the fire damage from Hesiesh\u2019s Gift.</li> <li>When a character begins their turn in short range of the sorcerer, they take [1/2 Essence, rounded up] points of initiative damage from the erupting flames. If they are in initiative crash, they instead take 1 level of lethal damage.</li> </ul><br /> A sorcerer who knows Hesiesh\u2019s Gift as her control spell adds two non-charm dice to their rolls against mundane heat hazards even when the spell is not active. When it is, she may choose whether or not characters in short range are affected by the aura.<br /> <br /> <i>Distortion (Goal Number: 15):</i> Distorting Hesieh\u2019s Gift of Divinity causes the sorcerer to be consumed by flames. A bondfire hazard appears at their current position, affecting all targets within short range.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>FIRE DRAGON\u2019S BLADE<br /> Cost</b>: 5sm, 1wp <br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None <br /> <b>Duration</b>: One Scene <br /> The sorcerer manifests a blade of flaming essence, drawn from the heart of the mighty dragons of fire. This blade is treated as a medium artifact weapon with the lethal and flame tags. It is compatible with Martial Arts styles that use blades.<br /> <br /> In addition, characters with an Essence pool gain access to the following powers while this spell is active:<ul><li><b>Iron-Breaking Inferno</b> (3m; Supplemental; Dual): The sorcerer\u2019s blade flares with sudden heat. If this ability is used to enhance a withering attack, the target loses two points of armored soak for the scene; if it is used to enhance a decisive attack, the target loses one point of armored hardness. This effect can stack with itself-- mundane armor whose soak is reduced to 0 in this manner is destroyed, while artifact armor repairs itself at scene end.</li> <li><b>Burning Essence Strike</b> (5m, 1 wp;, Supplemental; Decisive-only): When making a decisive attack with the Fire Dragon\u2019s Blade, the sorcerer may set aside any amount of her initiative. If her attack successfully deals damage, the target\u2019s very soul begins to burn. At the end of their next turn, add your essence to the pool of banked initiative and apply it as a second undodgeable, unblockable decisive attack which cannot be enhanced by charms.</li> </ul><br /> A sorcerer who knows Fire Dragon's Blade as her control spell can create and learn evocations for it.<br /> <br /> <i>Distortion (Goal Number: 12):</i> Distorting the Fire Dragon's Blade causes the sorcerer to be consumed by flames. A bondfire hazard appears at their current position, affecting all targets within short range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 09-26-2019, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T14:31:47-07:00","id":1338037,"title":"","content":"The AoE effect from <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>HESIESH\u2019S GIFT OF DIVINITY</b></span> which causes 5-9 ini damage every turn to every opponent in short range with no chance to resist feels too strong for a Terrestrial spell (multi-target attacks are extremely powerful in Exalted 3E).<br /> <br /> -consider adding a Stam Resist roll for opponents to avoid the effect.<br /> -consider adding an initiative cost to maintain the flames - effects that deal continuous damage or grant a major advantage tend to have that as a balancing factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T14:49:03-07:00","id":1338043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338030-solo-character-help-also-new-spells?p=1338037#post1338037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The AoE effect from <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>HESIESH\u2019S GIFT OF DIVINITY</b></span> which causes 5-9 ini damage every turn to every opponent in short range with no chance to resist feels too strong for a Terrestrial spell (multi-target attacks are extremely powerful in Exalted 3E).<br /> <br /> -consider adding a Stam Resist roll for opponents to avoid the effect.<br /> -consider adding an initiative cost to maintain the flames - effects that deal continuous damage or grant a major advantage tend to have that as a balancing factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like a really hard balancing point to hit because, if I understand the soak mechanics right, it'll wreck a bunch of bandits with Soak 3, but do absolutely nothing to a knight with Soak 10, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T15:07:49-07:00","id":1338046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338030-solo-character-help-also-new-spells?p=1338043#post1338043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like a really hard balancing point to hit because, if I understand the soak mechanics right, it'll wreck a bunch of bandits with Soak 3, but do absolutely nothing to a knight with Soak 10, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally Soak only applies to actual Withering Attacks. Special effects that damage initiative bypass Soak entirely, so your spell is a lot stronger than you thought.<br /> <br /> You could design the spell to be soakable mind you, it's just not how things normally work so you would have to state it in the text.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Edit : </i>Another thing to keep in mind is that special effects that damage initiative do not grant you the initiative the target loses unless explicitly mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 09-26-2019, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T15:28:14-07:00","id":1338051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338030-solo-character-help-also-new-spells?p=1338046#post1338046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Normally Soak only applies to actual Withering Attacks. Special effects that damage initiative bypass Soak entirely, so your spell is a lot stronger than you thought.<br /> <br /> You could design the spell to be soakable mind you, it's just not how things normally work so you would have to state it in the text.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Edit : </i>Another thing to keep in mind is that special effects that damage initiative do not grant you the initiative the target loses unless explicitly mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooohhhhh that makes it a lot better. What if I drop the damage to just [essence]?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T15:41:01-07:00","id":1338054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338030-solo-character-help-also-new-spells?p=1338051#post1338051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooooohhhhh that makes it a lot better. What if I drop the damage to just [essence]?</div> </div> </div> </div>Much better. At that point someone more knowledgeable about mechanics and balance might be better able to help you tune it further.<br /> <br /> My 2 cents would be that E4/E5 might still be worrisome, so I'd cap the effect at (lowest of Essence and 3) to be sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T02:02:01-07:00","id":1338121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338030-solo-character-help-also-new-spells#post1338030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Build</u></b><br /> <i>Note: The GM has already okay'd me using slashing swords with White Reaper style. Makes more sense than spears anyway.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>In a solo game, balance is not massively important.<br /> <br /> But you've created a combat monster -- one of the best fighters in existence. Then you've house ruled away one of the only balancing factors on the game's most powerful Martial Art to synergize it with one which covers all its weaknesses.<br /> <br /> (You also want to revisit your specailies -- you can't have an entire style, and only need one. &quot;White Reaper, Slashing swords&quot; for example.)<br /> <br /> In a solo game, this is probably ok. There's no other players to get jealous and you'll be soloing foes meant for an entire Circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T07:49:39-07:00","id":1338136,"title":"","content":"Yea I'm gonna have to second that. Single Point with White Reaper's defenses (and additional attack charms) is a terror to behold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T08:16:43-07:00","id":1338142,"title":"","content":"I mean... &quot;a terror to behold&quot; <i>is</i> kind of what I'm going for. And even without the houserule, I could mix in White Reaper because it can be used with no weapon, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T08:48:12-07:00","id":1338147,"title":"","content":"Your parry would be 1 lower when defending with White Reaper since you'd be barehanded (assuming your sword is a Medium weapon). More importantly, you wouldn't be able to use Charms of both styles to enhance the same attack or defense, because slashing swords and unarmed are 2 different weapons and attacks/defense always use a single weapon. Also less important but you'd need the Ambidextrous merit since you'd be attacking or defending with your off hand a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 09-27-2019, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T07:18:57-07:00","id":1338269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338030-solo-character-help-also-new-spells?p=1338142#post1338142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean... &quot;a terror to behold&quot; <i>is</i> kind of what I'm going for. And even without the houserule, I could mix in White Reaper because it can be used with no weapon, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No.<br /> <br /> From Core:<br /> <br /> <b>Single Point Shining Into the Void Weapons:</b> This style<br /> uses slashing swords and their artifact equivalents, reaper<br /> daiklaves, delivering lightning-fast attacks from the draw.<br /> <i><u><b>It cannot be used unarmed.</b></u></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T10:30:36-07:00","id":1338311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338030-solo-character-help-also-new-spells?p=1338121#post1338121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a solo game, this is probably ok. There's no other players to get jealous and you'll be soloing foes meant for an entire Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I\u2019d agree with this. It\u2019s overpowered but if you\u2019re fighting Alhat, a big battlegroup of his brides, their legendary commander and a pair of spirit aurochs you\u2019re not going to effortlessly destroy them or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}